libebml: swap_big(std::int32_t) returns sixteen bits on MSVC

`endian::swap_big(std::int32_t)` byte-swaps through `_byteswap_ulong` and then
reads the result back through a pointer to std::int16_t, so every 32-bit
big-endian value read on MSVC -- which is every four-byte float in a Matroska
file -- comes back as the low sixteen bits of its swapped image. GCC and Clang
take the __builtin_bswap32 branch and are right.

MediaPerch reads four-byte floats back from the file itself (modules/demux/mkv,
`float_of`) so it is right with or without this; the patch is here for whoever
updates the submodule. Against release-1.4.3-535-g928e273.

--- a/ebml/EbmlEndian.h
+++ b/ebml/EbmlEndian.h
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ static inline std::int32_t swap_big(std::int32_t value)
     return __builtin_bswap32(value);
 #else // _MSC_VER
     std::uint32_t res = _byteswap_ulong(*reinterpret_cast<std::uint32_t*>(&value));
-    return *reinterpret_cast<std::int16_t*>(&res);
+    return *reinterpret_cast<std::int32_t*>(&res);
 #endif
 }

